{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOver the MCP server, `claim_ticket` (`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:300-318`) stamps `(\"session\", resolve_session_id())` / `(\"harness\", resolve_harness())` from the **server process's** environment (`src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:71-72`; resolver `src/rebar/_commands/session_id.py:63`), so MCP-driven claims record no usable `claimed_session` and `cross_session_warning_for` (`src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py:45`) is silent for every MCP caller. The inbox feed (dependent child) needs a recipient identity on the mandated MCP path.\n\n## Approach\n\nResolve an **MCP acting-session identity** on the server as `principal` + optional `session_hint`, so a client can never select another principal.\n\n- **Principal seam (all strategies)**: the SDK's `mcp.server.auth.middleware.auth_context.get_access_token()`, a request-scoped ContextVar populated by `AuthContextMiddleware`, which `FastMCP.streamable_http_app()` installs whenever a token verifier is configured (rebar passes its composite at `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:615`). Every rebar verifier returns `AccessToken(client_id=...)`: static PAT (`src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:209-220`), JWKS (`:332`), introspection (`:504`), proxy (`:147`). So `principal = get_access_token().client_id` at tool-call time (one PAT per harness, `docs/mcp-client-setup.md:25-27`).\n- **Hint seam**: a new request header `X-Rebar-Session-Id`, captured by a new `SessionHintMiddleware` (`_mcp_auth.py`) into a new ContextVar `MCP_SESSION_HINT`, wired for **every** strategy by wrapping `mcp.streamable_http_app` with the proxy guard's method-assignment pattern (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py:628-638`), unconditionally. It records the hint, never authenticates. Validation: ≤128 chars, `[A-Za-z0-9._:-]`; else absent. The transport `Mcp-Session-Id` is deliberately not a fallback (it churns on reconnect and blue-green cutover, bug `aca0-6a66-0a27-47cf`).\n- **Resolver**: `current_mcp_identity() -> (principal, hint) | None` in `_mcp_auth.py`; `resolve_session_id()` gains one source ahead of `REBAR_SESSION_ID`, imported lazily inside the function (as `cross_session.py:40-43` does), returning `mcp:<principal>` or `mcp:<principal>/<hint>`; `resolve_harness()` returns `mcp:<principal>`. Without an MCP request context both ContextVars are unset and CLI/library behavior is byte-identical to today.\n- **Resolver consumers (all enumerated)**: `txn.py:71` claim stamp — migrated; `cross_session.py:45` — migrated, the warning fires over MCP with no reducer change (`_fold_claimed_session`, `src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py:25`, stores the string); `session_log.py:58/151/184` — the server-side session-log pointer rotates per MCP identity instead of one shared log; the count is bounded by distinct (principal, hint) pairs, session logs are already hidden from `list`/`ready` and graph health (`docs/event-schema.md`), no retire path is added (out of scope); `transition_close.py:785` — FORCE_CLOSE audit string shows the composite, cosmetic; `_cli/_llm_commands.py:172` — CLI-only, unaffected.\n- **Client recipes** (`docs/mcp-client-setup.md`, the three supported clients only): Claude Code — `headers: {\"X-Rebar-Session-Id\": \"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}\"}` beside the existing `Authorization: Bearer ${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLAUDE}`; Codex — `env_http_headers = { \"X-Rebar-Session-Id\" = \"REBAR_SESSION_ID\" }`, the key the Codex config reference (https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference, `mcp_servers.<id>.env_http_headers`: \"HTTP headers populated from environment variables when present\") defines beside the `bearer_token_env_var` already used at `docs/mcp-client-setup.md:115`; principal-only unless the operator sets that variable (Codex has no per-session variable, `session_id.py:31-33`); Copilot — principal-only in v1. Each recipe ships as \"supported\" only after the Step 1 probe returns a verdict for that client. Documented degradation: without a hint, all sessions of one principal share `mcp:<principal>`.\n\nPositive rationale: the SDK already carries the accepted principal per request and the proxy guard already shows how rebar wraps the ASGI app; reusing both adds no auth path and no schema change (`claimed_session`/`claim_harness` are existing nullable strings). Riskiest assumption, tested first: that each client actually sends the header — Claude Code's `${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}` expansion (open bugs anthropics/claude-code#6204, #51581) and Codex's `env_http_headers`. Step 1 is one throwaway probe per client against the deployed server with a temporary debug log line reading the hint back; each verdict decides whether that client's recipe ships as supported or principal-only. Rollout/rollback: additive (older server writes null, newer the composite; the detector handles both), so old and new images coexist during blue-green cutover; rollback is redeploying the previous image, no data cleanup.\n\nFailure disposition: a malformed or over-long hint is dropped (identity degrades to `mcp:<principal>`), never an error.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py` — `MCP_SESSION_HINT`, `SessionHintMiddleware`, `current_mcp_identity()`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/session_id.py` — MCP source ahead of the env-var chain in `resolve_session_id()` / `resolve_harness()`.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — unconditional `SessionHintMiddleware` wrap.\n- `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` (recipes), `docs/mcp-auth.md` (header semantics), `docs/session-id-shims.md` (correct the stale \"`CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is remote-only\" note — the local CLI exports it in 2.1.x), `docs/event-schema.md` (`claimed_session` value shape over MCP; session-log pointer effect).\n- `tests/unit/test_session_id.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_auth.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_claim_session.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit (pure): `resolve_session_id()` precedence matrix — MCP context with/without hint, malformed hint, no context → env chain unchanged (negative control).\n- Unit (middleware): valid header sets the ContextVar; absent/over-long/bad-charset leave it unset; installed under every strategy (static, jwks, proxy).\n- Contract (crosses both middlewares + tool + reducer): drive the real ASGI app from `mcp.streamable_http_app()` through `httpx.ASGITransport` with `Authorization: Bearer <static PAT>` and `X-Rebar-Session-Id`, so both middlewares run; `claim_ticket` then `show_ticket` reports `claimed_session == \"mcp:<client_id>/<hint>\"` and `claim_harness == \"mcp:<client_id>\"`; a second request under the same PAT with a different hint calling `comment_ticket` gets a non-null `cross_session_warning`; same hint → null (contrast).\n- Gate: all under `make test`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `claim_ticket` over the MCP ASGI app records `claimed_session` as `mcp:<client_id>/<hint>` when `X-Rebar-Session-Id` is sent and `mcp:<client_id>` when not; verified by `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_claim_session.py`.\n- [ ] `comment_ticket` over MCP from a different hint under the same PAT returns a non-null `cross_session_warning`, and the same hint returns null; verified by the contrast test in the same file.\n- [ ] A hint over 128 chars or outside `[A-Za-z0-9._:-]` is ignored and the claim still records `mcp:<client_id>`, and `SessionHintMiddleware` is present under the static, jwks, and proxy strategies; verified by `tests/unit/test_mcp_auth.py`.\n- [ ] Outside an MCP request, `resolve_session_id()` is unchanged for every existing env-var case; verified by `tests/unit/test_session_id.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` documents the `mcp:<principal>[/<hint>]` value shape and the session-log pointer effect, `docs/mcp-auth.md` documents the header as advisory and principal-scoped, and `docs/session-id-shims.md` no longer calls `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` remote-only; verified by grep assertions in `tests/unit/test_mcp_auth.py`.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The header probe verdict for Claude Code and for Codex (header received / not received, client version, timestamp) is recorded as a comment on this ticket before that client's recipe is marked supported in `docs/mcp-client-setup.md`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788563458052063001,"uuid":"563a5b75-6dfe-4cbb-a362-0ce1bf37bdde"}